{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4Lesv9ZEwiV9GumSzzy2U","type":"tool_result","content":"850:   *  THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel) */\n1289:Input.THIRDPERSON = {\n7090: *      each step: hero.update(dt, map, game.input) (with new E.Game({ input: 'THIRDPERSON' })), or for an AI an intent\n37: *    E.Mover on a TileMap of roofs climbs, vaults and leaps; E.ACTIONS, and E.sees / E.Suspicion for guards (17b-17d).\n7300: *      const seen = E.sees(guard, hero, { map, range: 120, fov: 1.6 });   // { seen, d, angle, exposure }\n7331:class Suspicion {\n7345:  /** one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state */\n8873:class Dialog {\n9029:class Menu {\n9163:class Shell {\n10657:  sees(a, b) { if (this.edges.some(([c, d]) => cross(a, b, c, d))) return false; return this.inside((a[0] + b[0]) / 2, (a[1] + b[1]) / 2); }\n10661:    if (this.sees(a, b)) return [a, b];\n10662:    const N = this.nodes; if (!this._links) this._links = N.map((p, i) => N.map((q, j) => j !== i && this.sees(p, q) ? hyp(p[0] - q[0], p[1] - q[1]) : -1));\n302:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n319:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel)\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181334__xac1bf5/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"61e4f93e-8f1a-4adc-beb5-34bfd90a85ce","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:15:15.711Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"850:   *  THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel) */\n1289:Input.THIRDPERSON = {\n7090: *      each step: hero.update(dt, map, game.input) (with new E.Game({ input: 'THIRDPERSON' })), or for an AI an intent\n37: *    E.Mover on a TileMap of roofs climbs, vaults and leaps; E.ACTIONS, and E.sees / E.Suspicion for guards (17b-17d).\n7300: *      const seen = E.sees(guard, hero, { map, range: 120, fov: 1.6 });   // { seen, d, angle, exposure }\n7331:class Suspicion {\n7345:  /** one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state */\n8873:class Dialog {\n9029:class Menu {\n9163:class Shell {\n10657:  sees(a, b) { if (this.edges.some(([c, d]) => cross(a, b, c, d))) return false; return this.inside((a[0] + b[0]) / 2, (a[1] + b[1]) / 2); }\n10661:    if (this.sees(a, b)) return [a, b];\n10662:    const N = this.nodes; if (!this._links) this._links = N.map((p, i) => N.map((q, j) => j !== i && this.sees(p, q) ? hyp(p[0] - q[0], p[1] - q[1]) : -1));\n302:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the code (nothing changes: free it first), or 'reserved' for the codes the menus keep (Escape, Enter, F keys, Start, the d-pad). The arrow keys and the d-pad always move as well\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n319:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n320:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, THIRDPERSON, SHMUP) has the moves (up, down, left, right) and the menu's actions (start, pause, confirm, cancel)\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181334__xac1bf5/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S4Lesv9ZEwiV9GumSzzy2U","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
