{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf8opiEaPBaxMSsphJ8x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Layouts hold on every viewport. Now I'll write the real About/credits data, rebuild, and generate and validate `exit-interview.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3774,"cache_read_input_tokens":265375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3774,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"fdf7d250-9d8e-4235-8425-62fca9806d65","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:34:55.046Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf8opJBLV2Wv8av6d5RP"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf8opiEaPBaxMSsphJ8x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SnpGScpvaMVSsVUnXNqQWV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"pkill -f \"http.server 8777\"; cd \"BurnNoticePending-TheWire-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181334\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nsi={\"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:13\",\"source\":\"The Wire (2002-2008), kept as gritty and real as the show. Original characters and places.\",\n\"genre\":\"Investigation / stealth / action-adventure (surveillance, listening and case-building, then a raid)\",\n\"perspective\":\"Three-quarter top-down (engine native); V or R3 switches to top-down or isometric. Menus and the wire room are flat screens.\",\n\"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 handoff (single-file engine, TileMap, Mover, Humanoid rigs, Suspicion, Dialog, Menu, Bullets, FlowField, canvas lighting, rain); AI Hub session client 1.3.0; plain JavaScript, no other libraries.\",\n\"artDirection\":\"Engine native pixel art at 320x240 expanded to any screen: HD-shaded Humanoid rigs, brick and plaster blocks, rain, streetlamp and flashlight lighting.\",\n\"animation\":\"Engine native: procedural Humanoid rigs (poses, expressions, live dialog portraits), tweened UI, particles, hit effects.\",\n\"audio\":\"All code-written: six synthesised music loops, synth sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices (a note per typed letter, pitched per speaker). No audio files.\",\n\"online\":\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode (1-4 players, own copy each, score reported); passes the hub harness check. No other networking.\",\n\"testing\":\"Headless Chromium and WebKit through Playwright: scripted full playthrough by the attract-mode AI, keyboard tests of photos, tip, tap, wire logging and raid, a mocked DualSense for axis inversion and glyphs, touch emulation, viewport-matrix (13 viewports, WebKit), hub harness. No real controller or iOS Safari.\",\n\"research\":\"Read the engine card, the stealth and adventure kits and the hub protocol. No web research on the show; written from general knowledge.\",\n\"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n\"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n\"usage\":\"unknown\"}\ntf=[\"About 9: an unreachable room (a table blocked a doorway), attract mode stalling on dialog, symbols the font cannot draw (several), cuff range lost after a shove, an enemy facing away with no gun, a menu hiding the title cast, a tagline cut off on phones, and a stale test server.\",\n\"2 critical: the blocked doorway made the raid unfinishable, and the demo froze on the judge's dialog.\",\n\"The attract-mode run: the demo plays the whole case, so one scripted pass hit every scene and found both critical bugs.\",\n\"Full-page screenshots of every viewport: only the title screen was reachable there, so they showed layout but few bugs.\"]\nef=[\"Humanoid rigs with live dialog portraits, and the free pause, settings, controls and glyph options; Mover, sees and Suspicion gave stealth almost for free.\",\n\"Yes. I guessed the font had pad symbols (it does not), that game.go switches at once (it fades first), and that input.tap is keyboard (it flips prompts to touch).\",\n\"The wire-room listening game, the case board, raid combat, the attract-mode driver, pixel-drawn pad symbols, and a gamepad axis-inversion shim.\",\n\"Building non-world screens: the canvas UI kit is thin for text-heavy or card screens, and FlowField treats any tall prop as a wall.\",\n\"The split between the canvas Menu and the HTML settings screens; one UI system would be simpler.\",\n\"Add built-in gamepad axis inversion and a font that includes controller face-button symbols.\"]\npf=[\"Clear deliverables, the controller-first rules, and the exit-interview JSON that tools read.\",\n\"Whether the source name includes the phrase after the dash, the 50-titles-then-RNG step (the list is not checkable), and how Online and Multiplayer differ.\",\n\"Scope: a feature-complete slice with attract mode, hub play and a 10-foot UI, tested only in headless browsers.\",\n\"Play the whole game start to finish with a real DualSense on a TV.\"]\nq={\"testing\":[\"How many issues did testing catch?\",\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\",\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\",\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"],\n\"engine\":[\"What did you like most about the engine?\",\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\",\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\",\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\",\"If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from engine, what would that be?\",\"If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\"],\n\"prompt\":[\"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\"What was confusing?\",\"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\"If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?\"]}\nd={\"sourceInformation\":si,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\"q\":q}\njson.dump(d,open('about-data.json','w'),indent=1)\nex={\"sourceInformation\":si,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\n\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"Burn Notice Pending\",\"tagline\":\"Nobody wins. Somebody clears a case.\",\"description\":\"A wiretap-detective game after The Wire: photograph a corner crew, pay an informant, tap a payphone, build the case for a judge, then serve the warrant. Gritty, slow-burn and original.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"Stealth\",\"source\":\"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\"series\":\"\",\"players\":\"1-4\",\"controls\":\"Stick/WASD move, L2/right mouse camera, X/E interact, Square/J shove, R1/Q shout, Triangle/Tab notebook\",\"tags\":[\"3d\",\"top-down\",\"story\",\"stealth\",\"retro\",\"pixel art\"]}}\njson.dump(ex,open('../exit-interview.json','w'),indent=1)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs && python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d))\" && cd /tmp/gh1 && python3 run.py \"$(cat F)\" shots/z '[[\"wait\",600],[\"js\",\"(()=>{__game.game.go(\\\"about\\\");return 1})()\"],[\"wait\",900],[\"key\",\"ArrowRight\"],[\"wait\",200],[\"key\",\"ArrowRight\"],[\"wait\",200],[\"key\",\"ArrowRight\"],[\"wait\",300],[\"shot\",\"ab\"]]'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3774,"cache_read_input_tokens":265375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3774,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"05204e1b-25f6-4d8a-ad15-3a87d40d8f90","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:35:10.731Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf8opJBLV2Wv8av6d5RP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SnpGScpvaMVSsVUnXNqQWV":{"command":"pkill -f \"http.server 8777\"; cd \"BurnNoticePending-TheWire-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181334\" && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nsi={\"date\":\"2026-11-02 18:13\",\"source\":\"The Wire (2002-2008), kept as gritty and real as the show. Original characters and places.\",\n\"genre\":\"Investigation / stealth / action-adventure (surveillance, listening and case-building, then a raid)\",\n\"perspective\":\"Three-quarter top-down (engine native); V or R3 switches to top-down or isometric. Menus and the wire room are flat screens.\",\n\"tech\":\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 handoff (single-file engine, TileMap, Mover, Humanoid rigs, Suspicion, Dialog, Menu, Bullets, FlowField, canvas lighting, rain); AI Hub session client 1.3.0; plain JavaScript, no other libraries.\",\n\"artDirection\":\"Engine native pixel art at 320x240 expanded to any screen: HD-shaded Humanoid rigs, brick and plaster blocks, rain, streetlamp and flashlight lighting.\",\n\"animation\":\"Engine native: procedural Humanoid rigs (poses, expressions, live dialog portraits), tweened UI, particles, hit effects.\",\n\"audio\":\"All code-written: six synthesised music loops, synth sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices (a note per typed letter, pitched per speaker). No audio files.\",\n\"online\":\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode (1-4 players, own copy each, score reported); passes the hub harness check. No other networking.\",\n\"testing\":\"Headless Chromium and WebKit through Playwright: scripted full playthrough by the attract-mode AI, keyboard tests of photos, tip, tap, wire logging and raid, a mocked DualSense for axis inversion and glyphs, touch emulation, viewport-matrix (13 viewports, WebKit), hub harness. No real controller or iOS Safari.\",\n\"research\":\"Read the engine card, the stealth and adventure kits and the hub protocol. No web research on the show; written from general knowledge.\",\n\"environment\":\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n\"model\":\"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n\"usage\":\"unknown\"}\ntf=[\"About 9: an unreachable room (a table blocked a doorway), attract mode stalling on dialog, symbols the font cannot draw (several), cuff range lost after a shove, an enemy facing away with no gun, a menu hiding the title cast, a tagline cut off on phones, and a stale test server.\",\n\"2 critical: the blocked doorway made the raid unfinishable, and the demo froze on the judge's dialog.\",\n\"The attract-mode run: the demo plays the whole case, so one scripted pass hit every scene and found both critical bugs.\",\n\"Full-page screenshots of every viewport: only the title screen was reachable there, so they showed layout but few bugs.\"]\nef=[\"Humanoid rigs with live dialog portraits, and the free pause, settings, controls and glyph options; Mover, sees and Suspicion gave stealth almost for free.\",\n\"Yes. I guessed the font had pad symbols (it does not), that game.go switches at once (it fades first), and that input.tap is keyboard (it flips prompts to touch).\",\n\"The wire-room listening game, the case board, raid combat, the attract-mode driver, pixel-drawn pad symbols, and a gamepad axis-inversion shim.\",\n\"Building non-world screens: the canvas UI kit is thin for text-heavy or card screens, and FlowField treats any tall prop as a wall.\",\n\"The split between the canvas Menu and the HTML settings screens; one UI system would be simpler.\",\n\"Add built-in gamepad axis inversion and a font that includes controller face-button symbols.\"]\npf=[\"Clear deliverables, the controller-first rules, and the exit-interview JSON that tools read.\",\n\"Whether the source name includes the phrase after the dash, the 50-titles-then-RNG step (the list is not checkable), and how Online and Multiplayer differ.\",\n\"Scope: a feature-complete slice with attract mode, hub play and a 10-foot UI, tested only in headless browsers.\",\n\"Play the whole game start to finish with a real DualSense on a TV.\"]\nq={\"testing\":[\"How many issues did testing catch?\",\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\",\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\",\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"],\n\"engine\":[\"What did you like most about the engine?\",\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\",\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\",\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\",\"If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from engine, what would that be?\",\"If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\"],\n\"prompt\":[\"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\"What was confusing?\",\"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\"If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?\"]}\nd={\"sourceInformation\":si,\"testingFeedback\":tf,\"engineFeedback\":ef,\"promptFeedback\":pf,\"q\":q}\njson.dump(d,open('about-data.json','w'),ind