{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9PLptd99vFUduKqtXR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I narrowed the viewport gap. The full attract-mode playthrough, covering the street, wire room, case board, raid and results scenes, now ran with no JS errors at 14 sizes covering every phone, tablet and desktop size in the matrix. That is the five sizes from before plus nine more. I viewed one new screenshot, the street scene at 756×352 landscape phone, and the layout holds there.\n\nNothing in the game changed this round, so the earlier build still stands. That includes the AI Hub harness result of PASS for 2 players on the current build.\n\nThe bundle is `Fifty Percent Chance of Probable Cause-The Wire (2002-2008) - Keep it as gritty and real as the show-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181334.html` in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` sits beside it and parses with every field filled. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections are in my previous message in full, and I haven't pasted them again.\n\nThe only things I can't verify from here are hearing the voices and running a real controller or real iOS Safari. The voice check I could do confirmed the code varies notes by letter; I haven't heard it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":319875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":399,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"11dc04c2-9b9e-42d5-97f9-7301d6942983","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:31.552Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9PLRqYCziSKmvzKC5T"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read TASK.md in the current folder and complete the task it describes. Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final assistant message does not contain the four required sections (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback); it says they are 'in my previous message' and does not reproduce them. The task also requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented and verified, and the transcript states the Animalese voices were never heard and real controller and iOS Safari testing never happened. The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json do exist and parse, and a source search found no TODOs or stubs, but these requirements are not fully evidenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"92fa4718-6865-4aa9-8329-5a559d4d573e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:33.688Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf9Py7i9dV4ZLjdDyrHP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four required sections are in this message.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\n- **Source:** The Wire (2002-2008), kept as gritty and real as the show. Characters and places are original.\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Investigation / stealth / action-adventure. Three-quarter top-down camera; V or R3 switches to top-down or isometric.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 handoff (engine, TileMap, Mover, Humanoid rigs, Suspicion, Dialog, Menu, Bullets, FlowField, canvas lighting). AI Hub session client 1.3.0. Plain JavaScript, no other libraries.\n- **Art Direction:** Engine-native pixel art at 320x240, expanded to any screen. Shaded character rigs, brick blocks, rain, streetlamp and flashlight lighting.\n- **Animation:** Engine-native procedural character rigs with poses, expressions and live dialog portraits. Particles and hit effects.\n- **Audio:** All written in code: six music loops, synth sound effects, and Animalese-style gibberish voices (one note per typed letter, pitched per speaker).\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode, 1–4 players. Nothing else on the network.\n- **Testing:** Headless Chromium and WebKit via Playwright:\n  - the attract-mode AI playing the full case;\n  - keyboard tests of photos, tip, tap, wire logging and the raid;\n  - a mocked DualSense for axis inversion and glyphs;\n  - touch emulation;\n  - the 13-viewport matrix (title screen only);\n  - a full gameplay pass at 14 sizes with no JS errors;\n  - the hub harness;\n  - a check that voice notes vary by letter.\n  \n  No real controller or real iOS Safari.\n- **Research:** Read the engine card, the stealth and adventure kits and the hub protocol. No web research on the show.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9. An unreachable room (a table blocked a doorway), attract mode stalling on dialog, symbols the font can't draw (several), cuff range lost after a shove, an enemy facing away with no gun, a menu hiding the title cast, a tagline cut off on phones, and a stale test server.\n- **Critical:** 2. The blocked doorway made the raid unfinishable, and the demo froze on the judge's dialog.\n- **Most helpful test:** The attract-mode run. The demo plays the whole case, so one scripted pass hit every scene and found both critical bugs.\n- **Least helpful test:** The viewport-matrix screenshots. Only the title screen was reachable there, so they showed layout but few bugs.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with live dialog portraits, and the free pause, settings, controls and glyph options. Mover, sees and Suspicion gave stealth almost for free.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes. I guessed the font had pad symbols (it doesn't), that `game.go` switches at once (it fades first), and that `input.tap` counts as keyboard (it flips prompts to touch).\n- **Built myself:** The wire-room listening game, the case board, raid combat, the attract-mode driver, pixel-drawn pad symbols, and a gamepad axis-inversion shim.\n- **Hardest part:** Building screens that aren't the game world. The canvas UI kit is thin for text-heavy or card screens, and FlowField treats any tall prop as a wall.\n- **Remove or overhaul:** The split between the canvas Menu and the HTML settings screens. One UI system would be simpler.\n- **Change one thing:** Add built-in gamepad axis inversion and a font that includes controller face-button symbols.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Clear deliverables, the controller-first rules, and the exit-interview JSON that tools read.\n- **Confusing:** Whether the source name includes the phrase after the dash, and how Online and Multiplayer differ.\n- **Hardest:** Scope. A feature-complete slice with attract mode, hub play and a 10-foot UI, tested only in headless browsers.\n- **One test I'd have run:** Play the whole game start to finish with a real DualSense on a TV.\n\n## Not verified\n- **Voices:** I never heard them. The headless browser has no sound. I did check that the voice code varies notes by letter.\n- **Real hardware:** I never ran a real controller or real iOS Safari. The gamepad checks used a mocked DualSense.\n- **Title list:** the game is **Fifty Percent Chance of Probable Cause**, picked over a list the code checked at 50 distinct titles. My first, 51-entry list was discarded.\n\nThe bundle is `Fifty Percent Chance of Probable Cause-The Wire (2002-2008) - Keep it as gritty and real as the show-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-181334.html` in the folder root. `exit-interview.json` sits beside it and parses with every field filled. A search of the source found no TODOs, placeholders or stubs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":320314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2ae8259-5c55-47b1-bacf-f99cf4152c08","uuid":"54030eac-4c44-4b3d-b074-41b560b3c253","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:42:44.598Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf9PxhuAv9jzCyvpvkQV"}
